The first step in the raw analysis process is to download the CSV files to analyze locally. Benjamin Hays identified the CSV files on public accessible GitHub repositories and wrote a script to download the CSV files to the main directory using Python\'92s built in urllib and named this file \'93download.py\'94. \
The next step is to analyze the downloaded files for size, dimensions, and encoding errors. The code for this was written by Tristen Garcia, and saved in a Python script called \'93analyze.py\'94. \
